{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-97eded76b91f95ae", "type": "tool_result", "content": "# Fish Audio S2 Technical Report\narXiv: 2603.08823\nAuthors: Shijia Liao, Yuxuan Wang, Songting Liu, Yifan Cheng, Ruoyi Zhang, Tianyu Li, Shidong Li, Yisheng Zheng, Xingwei Liu, Qingzheng Wang, Zhizhuo Zhou, Jiahua Liu, Xin Chen, Dawei Han\nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: tts_vc\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. A Dual-AR architecture that decouples temporal semantic modeling from depth-wise acoustic generation for efficient high-fidelity speech synthesis.\n  2. A dual-purpose data pipeline where speech quality and rich-transcription ASR models serve as both pre-training data filters and RL reward signals to eliminate distribution shift.\n  3. An RL-based post-training method using GRPO with multi-dimensional rewards to jointly optimize semantic accuracy, acoustic quality, and speaker similarity.\n  4. Native support for multi-speaker, multi-turn dialogue generation and stable long-form coherent audio synthesis.\n  5. Enhanced zero-shot instruction-following capabilities enabling fine-grained control over speech generation via natural language descriptions and inline vocal tags.\n  6. A production-ready SGLang-based inference engine achieving an RTF of 0.195 and a time-to-first-audio below 100 ms.\n  7. The introduction of the Fish Audio Instruction Benchmark to systematically evaluate fine-grained inline tag-following performance in TTS models.\n  8. The open-source release of the model weights, fine-tuning code, and inference engine to facilitate future TTS research.\n\nTags: TTS, TTS/架构-AR-LLM, TTS/功能-RL优化, TTS/控制-指令合成, TTS/功能-多说话人\n===\n# VoxCPM2 Technical Report\narXiv: 2606.06928\nAuthors: Yixuan Zhou, Guoyang Zeng, Xin Liu, Xiang Li, Renjie Yu, Jiancheng Gui, Jiaheng Wu, Ziyang Wang, Xudong Shen, Runchuan Ye, Zhisheng Zhang, Jiuyang Zhou, Bingsong Bai, Weiyue Sun, Mengyuan Deng, Qundong Shi, Zhiyong Wu, Zhiyuan Liu\nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: \nStatus: unread\n===\nPaper 2605.24618 not found\n===\n# DisCo-Speech: Controllable Zero-Shot Speech Generation with A Disentangled Speech Codec\narXiv: 2512.13251\nAuthors: Tao Li, Wenshuo Ge, Zhichao Wang, Zihao Cui, Yong Ma, Yingying Gao, Chao Deng, Shilei Zhang, Junlan Feng\nYear: 2025 | Venue: \nTopic: codec_vae\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. Introduction of DisCodec, a disentangled speech codec that explicitly factorizes speech into content, prosody, and timbre subspaces using parallel encoders and hybrid losses.\n  2. Development of a two-stage training paradigm that first achieves tri-factor disentanglement and then fuses content and prosody into unified, timbre-agnostic tokens while jointly optimizing reconstruction to mitigate the disentanglement-reconstruction trade-off.\n  3. Design of a zero-shot controllable TTS framework where a standard language model performs prosodic continuation and a decoder injects target timbre, enabling flexible independent control.\n  4. Demonstration of competitive voice cloning and superior zero-shot prosody control compared to existing state-of-the-art systems.\n\nTags: TTS, TTS/架构-AR-LLM, TTS/控制-参考语音, 压缩, 压缩/量化-FSQ, 压缩/语义声学-语义, 压缩/语义声学-声学", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "ae723d2c-4305-4e55-ac39-56b81999577a", "uuid": "f43d4975-115f-4d3c-9b79-6395f3899ba6", "timestamp": "2026-08-04T18:38:47.466Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "# Fish Audio S2 Technical Report\narXiv: 2603.08823\nAuthors: Shijia Liao, Yuxuan Wang, Songting Liu, Yifan Cheng, Ruoyi Zhang, Tianyu Li, Shidong Li, Yisheng Zheng, Xingwei Liu, Qingzheng Wang, Zhizhuo Zhou, Jiahua Liu, Xin Chen, Dawei Han\nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: tts_vc\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. A Dual-AR architecture that decouples temporal semantic modeling from depth-wise acoustic generation for efficient high-fidelity speech synthesis.\n  2. A dual-purpose data pipeline where speech quality and rich-transcription ASR models serve as both pre-training data filters and RL reward signals to eliminate distribution shift.\n  3. An RL-based post-training method using GRPO with multi-dimensional rewards to jointly optimize semantic accuracy, acoustic quality, and speaker similarity.\n  4. Native support for multi-speaker, multi-turn dialogue generation and stable long-form coherent audio synthesis.\n  5. Enhanced zero-shot instruction-following capabilities enabling fine-grained control over speech generation via natural language descriptions and inline vocal tags.\n  6. A production-ready SGLang-based inference engine achieving an RTF of 0.195 and a time-to-first-audio below 100 ms.\n  7. The introduction of the Fish Audio Instruction Benchmark to systematically evaluate fine-grained inline tag-following performance in TTS models.\n  8. The open-source release of the model weights, fine-tuning code, and inference engine to facilitate future TTS research.\n\nTags: TTS, TTS/架构-AR-LLM, TTS/功能-RL优化, TTS/控制-指令合成, TTS/功能-多说话人\n===\n# VoxCPM2 Technical Report\narXiv: 2606.06928\nAuthors: Yixuan Zhou, Guoyang Zeng, Xin Liu, Xiang Li, Renjie Yu, Jiancheng Gui, Jiaheng Wu, Ziyang Wang, Xudong Shen, Runchuan Ye, Zhisheng Zhang, Jiuyang Zhou, Bingsong Bai, Weiyue Sun, Mengyuan Deng, Qundong Shi, Zhiyong Wu, Zhiyuan Liu\nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: \nStatus: unread\n===\nPaper 2605.24618 not found\n===\n# DisCo-Speech: Controllable Zero-Shot Speech Generation with A Disentangled Speech Codec\narXiv: 2512.13251\nAuthors: Tao Li, Wenshuo Ge, Zhichao Wang, Zihao Cui, Yong Ma, Yingying Gao, Chao Deng, Shilei Zhang, Junlan Feng\nYear: 2025 | Venue: \nTopic: codec_vae\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. Introduction of DisCodec, a disentangled speech codec that explicitly factorizes speech into content, prosody, and timbre subspaces using parallel encoders and hybrid losses.\n  2. Development of a two-stage training paradigm that first achieves tri-factor disentanglement and then fuses content and prosody into unified, timbre-agnostic tokens while jointly optimizing reconstruction to mitigate the disentanglement-reconstruction trade-off.\n  3. Design of a zero-shot controllable TTS framework where a standard language model performs prosodic continuation and a decoder injects target timbre, enabling flexible independent control.\n  4. Demonstration of competitive voice cloning and superior zero-shot prosody control compared to existing state-of-the-art systems.\n\nTags: TTS, TTS/架构-AR-LLM, TTS/控制-参考语音, 压缩, 压缩/量化-FSQ, 压缩/语义声学-语义, 压缩/语义声学-声学", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}}
